"""Regenerate the sources page from local snapshot metadata."""
import json,html
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
a=json.loads((root/'data/amenities.json').read_text());g=json.loads((root/'data/green-cover.json').read_text());r=json.loads((root/'data/living-cost.json').read_text());s=json.loads((root/'data/search-places.json').read_text())
cpcb='https://cpcb.nic.in/openpdffile.php?id=UmVwb3J0RmlsZXMvMTY2OV8xNzI3NDE0NTc1X21lZGlhcGhvdG8yOTAyNy5wZGY%3D'
body=f'''<header><a href="../">← Back to the ward map</a><a href="../vision/">Our vision →</a></header><main>
<div class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">DATA, PEOPLE & METHODS</p><h1>Where our map comes from</h1><p>Credit to the people who collected and shared the data. Here is what we use, when it was observed, and what our calculations can tell you.</p><small>Documentation updated 11 October 2026 · Local prototype snapshots</small></div>
<nav aria-label="Source sections"><a href="#boundaries">Boundaries</a><a href="#osm">OpenStreetMap</a><a href="#rent">Living costs</a><a href="#green">Green cover</a><a href="#noise">Measured noise</a><a href="#methods">Our methods</a></nav>
<section id="boundaries"><p class="eyebrow">BOUNDARIES & POPULATION ATTRIBUTES</p><h2>OpenCity, GBA & Bharat Atlas</h2><p><a href="https://data.opencity.in/dataset/gba-wards-delimitation-2025">OpenCity’s GBA ward delimitation dataset</a>, distributed as a <a href="https://bharatlas.com/view/wards_bengaluru_gba">Bharat Atlas GeoJSON export</a>. Our map uses 369 wards across five corporations, with the November 2025 boundary edition.</p><dl><dt>Local data</dt><dd><a href="../data/wards-bengaluru-gba.geojson">Ward GeoJSON</a> · <a href="../data/assemblies.geojson">Derived constituency outlines</a></dd><dt>Our changes</dt><dd>Corrected the export’s reversed coordinate order to GeoJSON longitude, latitude. Dissolved wards by assembly constituency number/name: 28 outlines, clipped to GBA. These are not separate official full constituency boundaries.</dd><dt>Population</dt><dd>The boundary export includes legacy census fields displayed as 2011 population. Their allocation to the new wards has not been independently verified; they are not current population estimates.</dd><dt>Reuse</dt><dd>See the OpenCity dataset’s resource licence and publisher notes. The downloaded export does not carry a separate licence field. OSM licensing below applies to OSM data, not automatically to these boundaries.</dd></dl></section>
<section id="osm"><p class="eyebrow">AMENITIES, TRANSPORT, ROADS & PLACE SEARCH</p><h2>OpenStreetMap contributors</h2><p>Community mapping provides amenity locations, station objects, metro route geometry, roads, industrial/waste sites, the airport location and named buildings/localities. Downloaded with <a href="https://overpass-api.de/">Overpass API</a>; the app uses local snapshots.</p><dl><dt>Dates</dt><dd>Amenities: {html.escape(a['osmTimestamp'])}. Roads/sites: {html.escape(a['exposureMetadata']['roadsTimestamp'])}. Metro routes: {html.escape(a['metroRouteMetadata']['osmTimestamp'])}. Destination directory: {html.escape(s['osmTimestamp'])}.</dd><dt>Local data</dt><dd><a href="../data/amenities.json">Amenity and ward aggregates</a> · <a href="../data/search-places.json">Named destination directory</a>. Raw road geometry is processed locally and is not bundled.</dd><dt>Licence / credit</dt><dd>© OpenStreetMap contributors. Data under <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">Open Database License (ODbL)</a>. Attribution and share-alike obligations apply to distributed adaptations.</dd><dt>Our changes</dt><dd>Assign point and geometry-centre objects to wards; classify OSM tags; count mapped objects; calculate straight-line distances. Metro station line assignments use route membership or a stop/platform within 250 m. The match method is shown in station popups.</dd><dt>Limitations</dt><dd>Missing tags and duplicate point/area representations affect counts. Area centres may not be entrances. Explicit public-park access tags are sparse. Nearest sites outside the buffered download can be missing. Distances are from a ward representative point, not every home or a route.</dd></dl><p>The map background uses OpenStreetMap raster tiles with on-map attribution. <a href="https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/">Tile service policy</a> is separate from the database licence. Place queries search the bundled directory locally.</p></section>
<section id="rent"><p class="eyebrow">CROWDSOURCED RENT + YOUR EXPENSE ASSUMPTIONS</p><h2>bengaluru.rent · Harshit Anand</h2><p>The <a href="https://bengaluru.rent/bengaluru-rent-index">October 2026 Bengaluru Rent Index</a> reports locality rent medians by home size, from tenant reports in the 90 days ending 6 October 2026. Its published tables require at least 15 reports per locality/home-size group. The publisher permits reuse with attribution.</p><dl><dt>Download</dt><dd><a href="https://bengaluru.rent/data/bengaluru-rent-index-2026-10.csv">Publisher CSV</a> · <a href="../data/rent-index-2026-10.csv">Local CSV snapshot</a> · <a href="../data/living-cost.json">Our geographic matches</a></dd><dt>Ward approximation</dt><dd>Closest OSM locality centre within 2 km of the ward representative point, using the requested BHK median. OSM centres may differ from the rent publisher’s centres. Sarjapur Road is omitted because the corridor has no unambiguous centre.</dd><dt>Coverage</dt><dd>67 wards for 1 BHK; 115 for 2 BHK; 7 for 3 BHK. All other wards have unavailable rent data.</dd><dt>Living cost</dt><dd>Locality rent + your non-rent monthly expense allowance. Score = max(0, 1 − estimated cost / (2 × budget)). This is a household spending scenario, not a ward-wide price survey or income prediction. Deposits and moving costs are excluded.</dd><dt>Ranking</dt><dd>When living cost has a positive custom-index weight, missing-rent wards receive no total score and cannot benefit from renormalizing away affordability.</dd></dl></section>
<section id="green"><p class="eyebrow">SATELLITE VEGETATION DISPLAY & OUR WARD PROXY</p><h2>bengaluru.rent + Copernicus Sentinel-2</h2><p><a href="https://bengaluru.rent/">bengaluru.rent</a> publishes a vegetation visualization from Sentinel-2, attributed to Copernicus and dated 28 March 2026. Credit to Harshit Anand for making the processed layer available.</p><p class="credit">Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel-2 data [2026]</p><dl><dt>Data</dt><dd><a href="https://bengaluru.rent/greenery-overlay.webp">Publisher vegetation raster</a> · <a href="../data/greenery-overlay.webp">Local raster</a> · <a href="../data/green-cover.json">Our ward summaries</a>. Retrieved {html.escape(g['retrievedAt'])}. SHA-256: <code>{g['sha256']}</code></dd><dt>Extent & resolution</dt><dd>Latitude 12.82–13.12, longitude 77.45–77.78. Display raster: 600 × 556 pixels, approximately 60 m per pixel. This is the published visualization’s resolution, not a claim about the original satellite product.</dd><dt>Ward calculation</dt><dd>Mean alpha (display opacity) of pixel centres inside the ward, weighted by cosine of latitude. Divide by the largest covered-ward mean to obtain a 0–1 relative score. Require at least 95% of the ward’s extent inside the raster. 366 of 369 wards have a score; 3 remain unavailable.</dd><dt>What it means</dt><dd>Stronger published vegetation-display signal scores higher. It is not calibrated NDVI, percentage tree canopy, publicly accessible greenery, shade on footpaths or a biodiversity measure. Trees, grass and other vegetation can all contribute. The source’s cloud/no-data mask and processing thresholds are not supplied; transparent pixels count as zero display signal.</dd><dt>Credit & terms</dt><dd>Underlying Sentinel data is free and open under the <a href="https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/documents/247904/690755/Sentinel_Data_Legal_Notice">Copernicus Sentinel legal notice</a>. The processed visualization is credited to bengaluru.rent; our ward aggregation is a further derived proxy. We do not reproduce the publisher’s website code.</dd></dl></section>
<section id="noise"><p class="eyebrow">HISTORICAL MEASUREMENTS · CONTEXT ONLY</p><h2>Central Pollution Control Board</h2><p>The measured-noise table reproduces Bengaluru station values from table 5.5 of the <a href="{cpcb}">CPCB Annual Report 2022–23</a>: day/night annual averages for 2022. It is not a live feed.</p><p>These station observations are displayed as historical context. They do not establish noise across every ward, are not interpolated, and do not calibrate our road-pressure score. The source report does not state a separate open-data licence in the records used here; values are attributed to CPCB.</p></section>
<section id="methods"><p class="eyebrow">COMPUTATIONS & CURATION BY THIS PROTOTYPE</p><h2>Our scores are models, not independent observations</h2><ul><li><strong>Counts:</strong> mapped count divided by the largest ward count; sparse public-access tags stay visibly limited.</li><li><strong>Proximity:</strong> score falls linearly with straight-line distance to a mapped destination, up to the metric’s stated threshold. Reverse preference is available.</li><li><strong>Noise proxy:</strong> clipped road length × estimated carriageway width × road-class factor, divided by ward area. Tagged widths take priority; otherwise lanes × 3.2 m or class defaults. This is infrastructure intensity, not measured decibels.</li><li><strong>Industrial/waste proximity:</strong> distance to a mapped site centre, not its boundary, emissions, operational status or odour exposure.</li><li><strong>Within-ward essentials:</strong> presence of healthcare, pharmacy, park and bus stop groups, divided by four. It does not measure walkability.</li><li><strong>Custom index:</strong> weighted average of available normalized components. Cost has the special missing-data rule above. A high weight changes contribution, not the underlying count. Rankings follow current ward filters; ties are ordered by ward name.</li><li><strong>Presets:</strong> editable preference weights and household spending scenarios. They are not surveys or predictions of income by age.</li></ul><p>Metro journey time, footpath quality, live flood/pothole conditions and validated smell/noise exposure remain unavailable. Sources listed here do not make those metrics measured.</p><p><a href="../README.md">Project README</a> documents formulas and refresh scripts. Snapshots are not automatically refreshed; new data can change rankings even with unchanged weights.</p></section>
<section id="references"><p class="eyebrow">REFERENCE MATERIAL · NOT LIVE DATA FEEDS</p><h2>Agency references & software</h2><p><a href="https://www.bmrc.co.in/schematic-route-map/">BMRCL schematic route map</a> is the official transport reference; our mapped route geometry is from OSM. <a href="https://apps.bbmpgov.in/SWM/Home/Documents/ReportsandStudies/How%20to%20process%20wet%20wastehandbook.pdf">BBMP wet-waste handbook</a> provides historical KCDC context, not current odour measurements.</p><p><a href="https://leafletjs.com/">Leaflet 1.9.4</a> powers the map (BSD-2-Clause), loaded from the unpkg CDN. Python/Shapely/Pillow/NumPy support local data processing. No Google Maps data is included.</p></section>
<footer>Thanks to OpenCity, GBA, Bharat Atlas, OpenStreetMap contributors, Harshit Anand / bengaluru.rent, Copernicus and CPCB.<br><a href="../">Return to the map →</a></footer></main>'''
style='''*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f5f7f2;color:#1d3027;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif;line-height:1.65}a{color:#196e4b;text-underline-offset:3px}header{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:20px max(24px,calc((100vw - 940px)/2));background:#fff;border-bottom:1px solid #dce5db;font-size:12px}header span{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:1.5px;font-weight:700}main{max-width:940px;padding:30px 24px 50px;margin:auto}.hero{padding:18px 0 26px}.eyebrow{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:1.5px;font-weight:750;color:#2c7a57}h1{font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,48px);line-height:1.12;letter-spacing:-1.5px;margin:12px 0 20px}.hero>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:650px;font-size:17px;color:#5b6c61}.hero small{color:#718076}nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin-bottom:28px}nav a{border:1px solid #ceddce;background:#fff;padding:7px 12px;border-radius:20px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none}section{background:#fff;border:1px solid #dce5db;border-radius:14px;padding:25px 28px;margin:18px 0;scroll-margin-top:20px}h2{font-size:23px;line-height:1.3;margin:7px 0 17px}p,li{font-size:14px}dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:145px 1fr;gap:12px 20px;font-size:13px;margin-top:24px}dt{font-weight:700;color:#526657}dd{margin:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}code{font-size:10px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.credit{background:#eaf4e8;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 15px;font-weight:650}li{margin:12px 0}footer{padding:28px 5px;font-size:12px;color:#66786b}footer a{display:inline-block;margin-top:15px}@media(max-width:600px){main{padding:20px 14px}section{padding:20px 18px}dl{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:4px}dd{margin-bottom:14px}header span{display:none}}'''
(root/'sources/index.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Sources & methods — Bengaluru Life Index</title><style>'+style+'</style></head><body>'+body+'</body></html>')
